From 6df8957a59fe489c37cb2aed7c74bd9ebaed9a14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 06:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 100/112] context : SiegeLadder D15 v2 - a call's last N tokens
 always go narrow, the automatic mode halves the encoder-only width too, and a
 reserve no longer repeats what failed before. (1) The plan's wide part ends N
 tokens before the call's end (and at P4's limit, as before): a call that fits
 one whole-model ubatch stays one - v1 cut a 2.8K agent turn at C7's bound
 into a wide part and a 140-row tail, a second pass over the experts (8.8 s
 against 7.6 at 128K, now 7.7). (2) When P4's encoder-only graph does not fit
 at -ub either (256K at -ub 8192: 9.4 GiB), its width halves down to the whole
 model's (llama_context::d15_ub_wide): 256K at -ub 8192 reads its document at
 854 tok/s against 741 at today's 3072 (+15%), 128K at 1215 against 756
 (+61%). (3) Every phase change of P1 reserves again: the graph sizes of D15
 are logged once per width pair, and a non-sparse (D10) graph whose full
 widths did not fit once is reserved capped at once from then on
 (llama_context::d12_capped) - at 256K a reserve took 1.6-2.5 s against
 0.2-0.75 without D15, a turn +1.7 s. Logits byte for byte where the layouts
 coincide (prompt 16 896 = 8 x 2048 + 512 at -ub 2048 / N 512), and the path
 without D15 byte for byte as before (18K at -ub 2048) (SiegeLadder runs.md
 4.252-4.254)

---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 81 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 src/llama-context.h   |  4 +++
 2 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
